course: dictionary
lesson: 12251
title: Constraint: the rules and limits
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A constraint is a limit. It is something that stops you doing everything you want, or a rule you must follow. «Our class had time constraints, so we had only twenty minutes to finish the poster.» The time was limited, so the children had to work fast.
explain: In maths, a constraint is a rule the answer must obey. «Find a whole number under 10 that is a multiple of 4.» The constraints are whole number, under 10 and multiple of 4. Any answer that breaks one of them is wrong.
explain: In design, a constraint is a condition a design must follow, such as budget, size or materials. «The bag must cost under £5 and fit in a box.» Those are budget and size constraints. Look for clue words like must, only, under and limit to spot a constraint in a text.
fact: A constraint is something that limits or controls what you can do.
fact: «Time constraints» means there is only a set amount of time to do something.
fact: «Budget constraints» means there is only a set amount of money to spend.
fact: In maths and design, a constraint is a rule or condition that the answer or design must follow.
fact: «Under constraint» means forced or held back by a limit.
exercise: «Our club had strict time constraints, so we finished early.» What does constraints mean here? | Lots of spare time to play | *Limits that controlled how long we had | Rules about the colour of the paper | Friends who helped us with the work
exercise: Maths problem: «Find a whole number under 10.» What is the constraint in this problem? | The answer must be written in words | *The answer must be a whole number under 10 | The answer is the biggest number possible | The answer must be a fraction
exercise: Design brief: «The bag must cost under £5 and have a zip.» What is the budget constraint? | The bag was made by a child | The bag must have a zip | *The bag must cost under £5 | The bag is blue
test: Which phrase means there is only a set amount of time to do something? | open spaces | *time constraints | happy feelings | colour choices
test: What is a constraint in maths or design? | *A rule or condition the answer or design must follow | A loud sound in the hall | A prize for winning the task | A kind of bird found in the park
exam: Choose the best meaning of constraint. | Something that always makes things easier | A colour used in a painting | *Something that limits what you can do | A type of music played at school
